# TLSFlow License Notice

Version: 2026-08-23

TLSFlow is a composite project containing different types of content. This root
`LICENSE` file describes the default licensing scope for each category. If a file,
directory, or third-party component includes a more specific `LICENSE`, `COPYING`,
`NOTICE`, SPDX identifier, or other licensing notice, that notice controls. When
content falls into more than one category, the order of precedence is: the specific
file notice, third-party/community plugin notice, extension-contract scope,
documentation and examples scope, and finally the default license for core source.

## Content and License Mapping

| Content scope | Default license | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| TLSFlow core source and official implementations distributed with the repository | PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 | Noncommercial use is permitted; commercial use requires a separate commercial license or EULA. |
| Plugin SDK, Manifest, Host API contracts, and their schema/protocol examples | Apache-2.0 | These extension interfaces are licensed under Apache License 2.0, including its patent grant. |
| Third-party or community plugins | Chosen by the plugin author | Each plugin must include its own license and third-party notices; this file does not grant a unified license to community plugins. |
| TLSFlow documentation and examples | CC BY 4.0 | Redistribution, adaptation, and republication are permitted with attribution, a license link, and a description of changes. Third-party materials remain subject to their own licenses. |

### Core Source Scope

Unless a file or directory states otherwise, TLSFlow core source includes the platform
backend, Web console, official Agents, runtimes, compatibility implementations, build
and deployment code, and official built-in plugins distributed with the repository.
The default license for core source is the complete PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0
license below.

### Extension Contract Scope

The plugin SDK, Manifest, Host API contracts, and their public schemas, protocol
definitions, and accompanying protocol examples are licensed under Apache-2.0 by
default. This grant covers only those extension interfaces and contract materials; it
does not automatically relicense the TLSFlow core implementation under Apache-2.0 or
change the original license of any third-party component.

### Commercial Use

PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 does not grant commercial-use rights. Before using,
deploying, providing a commercial service with, or distributing restricted core source,
commercial customers must obtain a separate commercial license or end-user license
agreement (EULA) from the rights holder. A commercial license or EULA covers core
source, versions, features, support, and plugin rights only to the extent expressly
specified in that agreement.

### Copyright and Contributions

Copyright in each file belongs to its respective author or rights holder. Unless a
contribution agreement or file notice states otherwise, contributed material is subject
to the default license for its applicable content scope under this file. A contribution
does not grant commercial rights beyond that scope.

